## Features

GUTS IAM provides a comprehensive identity, access, and security control system designed to manage authentication, authorization, and security monitoring in a centralized way.

It also includes additional security mechanisms such as email verification, password recovery, session control, and early-stage fraud detection signals.

---

### Authentication

Handles secure user identity verification and access control.

- Secure user login system
- JWT-based authentication for stateless sessions
- Password encryption and secure credential storage
- Token validation for protected endpoints
- Prevents unauthorized access attempts

---

### User Management

Manages user accounts and lifecycle operations.

- Create and register users
- Update user profile information
- Enable or disable accounts
- Maintain user status and activity tracking
- Centralized identity control

---

### Role & Permission Management

Implements structured access control using RBAC.

- Create and manage roles
- Assign roles to users
- Define system permissions
- Map permissions to roles
- Enforce authorization at runtime

---

### Session Management

Ensures controlled and secure user sessions.

- Session tracking and validation
- Token-based session handling
- Session expiry control
- Secure logout mechanism

---

### Token System

Improves security and user experience through token lifecycle management.

- Access token generation using JWT
- Refresh token support for session renewal
- Secure token validation and expiration handling

---

### Email Verification & Password Recovery

Provides account security and recovery mechanisms.

- Email verification during registration
- Secure password reset via email link
- Time-bound reset tokens
- Prevents unauthorized account recovery attempts

---

### Location Tracking (Security Layer)

Adds an additional security signal layer for anomaly detection.

- Capture login location metadata (IP-based)
- Track login patterns across locations
- Support future fraud detection model integration (ML-based system planned)
- Helps identify suspicious or unusual access behavior

---

### Audit Logging

Tracks all critical system activities for transparency and monitoring.

- Record user and admin actions
- Store security-relevant events
- Maintain historical audit trail
- Support export for reporting and compliance
